  "grammar_points": [
    {
      "name": "命令形 (meireikei - imperative)",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N4",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "How it works: The imperative form creates direct commands. For godan verbs (-u verbs), change the final vowel to -e. For ichidan verbs (-ru verbs), replace る with ろ.\n\nExample from this song: 目覚めろ (mezamero) = 'wake up!' — from 目覚める (mezameru, 'to awaken'), an ichidan verb → drop る, add ろ. Also: 燃やせ (moyase) = 'set ablaze!' — from 燃やす (moyasu, 'to burn'), a godan verb → す becomes せ\n\nMore examples:\n• 立つ (tatsu, 'to stand') → 立て (tate, 'stand up!')\n• 見る (miru, 'to see') → 見ろ (miro, 'look!')\n• 来る (kuru, 'to come') → 来い (koi, 'come!') — irregular\n\nNote: This form is very strong and direct, common in anime, songs, and sports cheering. Irregular verbs: する (suru) → しろ (shiro), 来る (kuru) → 来い (koi)."
      },
      "conjugation_path": "目覚める (mezameru, 'to awaken') → 目覚めろ (mezamero, 'wake up!') / 燃やす (moyasu, 'to burn') → 燃やせ (moyase, 'set ablaze!')"
    },
    {
      "name": "〜ても (temo - even if)",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N4",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "How it works: Add ても (temo) after a verb's te-form to express 'even if' or 'even though.' The result doesn't change regardless of the condition stated.\n\nExample from this song: 焦がれても (kogarete mo) = 'even if I yearn' — from 焦がれる (kogareru, 'to yearn for') → 焦がれて (kogarete) + も (mo)\n\nMore examples:\n• 雨が降っても行く (ame ga futte mo iku, 'I'll go even if it rains') — from 降る (furu, 'to rain')\n• 失敗しても大丈夫 (shippai shite mo daijoubu, 'even if you fail, it's OK') — from 失敗する (shippai suru, 'to fail')\n• 高くても買う (takakute mo kau, 'I'll buy it even if it's expensive') — i-adjective form\n\nNote: For verbs → te-form + も. For i-adjectives → change い to くても. For na-adjectives/nouns → でも."
      },
      "conjugation_path": "焦がれる (kogareru, 'to yearn') → 焦がれて (kogarete) → 焦がれても (kogarete mo, 'even if yearning')"
    },
    {
      "name": "〜のは〜だ (no wa ~ da - emphasis)",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N4",
      "explanation": {
        "en": "How it works: This cleft sentence structure emphasizes one part of the sentence. Verb + のは (no wa) turns the action into a topic, and だ (da) identifies it. Pattern: 'The thing that does X is Y.'\n\nExample from this song: 僕を強くするのは仲間の絆 (boku o tsuyoku suru no wa nakama no kizuna) = 'what makes me strong is the bond with my companions' — the のは highlights 'the thing that makes me strong'\n\nMore examples:\n• 好きなのは音楽だ (suki na no wa ongaku da, 'what I like is music') — emphasizing the object\n• 大切なのは気持ちだ (taisetsu na no wa kimochi da, 'what's important is feelings') — emphasizing importance\n• 教えてくれたのは先生だ (oshiete kureta no wa sensei da, 'the one who taught me was the teacher') — emphasizing the person\n\nNote: の nominalizes the verb clause (turns it into a noun phrase). This structure is used when you want to say 'the one who / the thing that / what...'"
      },
      "conjugation_path": "僕を強くする (boku o tsuyoku suru, 'makes me strong') + のは (no wa) + 仲間の絆 (nakama no kizuna, 'bond with companions')"
    },
    {
      "name": "意志形 〜よう (volitional form)",
      "jlpt_reference": "JLPT N4",
      "explanation": {
